{
  "id": "agent-501",
  "name": "Agent 501 · Multi-Agent Review",
  "description": "Two agents on one input — Explain (agent-101) and Review (agent-201) fan out from a Java cell, then a Java cell combines both. Run the pipeline.",
  "metadata": {
    "category": "tutorial",
    "subcategory": "Agents & Skills",
    "language": "agent",
    "level": 501
  },
  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "a501-md",
      "type": "MARKDOWN",
      "mode": "jshell",
      "source": "# Agent 501 · Multi-Agent Review\n\nA single input drives **two** agents in parallel steps, then a Java cell merges their answers:\n\n- `code-input` (Java) prints a snippet.\n- `explain` (Agent · agent-101) explains it → binds `explanation`.\n- `review`  (Agent · agent-201) reviews it → binds `reviewNotes`.\n- `combine` (Java) prints both.\n\nRun the **pipeline** to see code and multiple agents interwork in one graph.",
      "output": "",
      "executed": false
    },
    {
      "id": "a501-input",
      "type": "CODE",
      "mode": "jshell",
      "anchor": "code-input",
      "source": "//@ anchor: code-input\n// One anchored cell feeds two agents. Both of the agent cells below declare\n// //@ depends: code-input and pull this cell in with {{code-input}}, which\n// resolves to what the cell *printed* - so the println at the bottom is what\n// actually reaches them.\n//\n// \"\"\" opens a Java text block: a multi-line literal that preserves line breaks\n// and strips the shared indentation, which is what lets a code sample be pasted\n// in unescaped.\nString code = \"\"\"\n    boolean isPrime(int n) {\n        if (n < 2) return false;\n        for (int i = 2; i < n; i++) if (n % i == 0) return false;\n        return true;\n    }\n    \"\"\";\n\n// This method is correct but naive - it trial-divides all the way up to n rather\n// than stopping at sqrt(n). Correct-but-slow is deliberate here: it gives the\n// explainer agent something clear to describe and the reviewer something to\n// criticise, from the very same input.\nSystem.out.println(code);",
      "output": "",
      "executed": false
    },
    {
      "id": "a501-explain",
      "type": "CODE",
      "mode": "agent",
      "anchor": "explain",
      "dependsOn": [
        "code-input"
      ],
      "source": "//@ anchor: explain\n//@ depends: code-input\n//@ agent: agent-101\n//@ bind: explanation\nExplain this method in two short sentences:\n\n{{code-input}}",
      "output": "",
      "executed": false
    },
    {
      "id": "a501-review",
      "type": "CODE",
      "mode": "agent",
      "anchor": "review",
      "dependsOn": [
        "code-input"
      ],
      "source": "//@ anchor: review\n//@ depends: code-input\n//@ agent: agent-201\n//@ bind: reviewNotes\nReview this method for correctness and efficiency, briefly:\n\n{{code-input}}",
      "output": "",
      "executed": false
    },
    {
      "id": "a501-combine",
      "type": "CODE",
      "mode": "jshell",
      "anchor": "combine",
      "dependsOn": [
        "explain",
        "review"
      ],
      "source": "//@ anchor: combine\n//@ depends: explain, review\n// Two anchors on one //@ depends: line means both must finish before this cell\n// runs. Neither agent depends on the other, so the graph fans out from\n// code-input, runs them independently, and only rejoins here - a fan-out/fan-in\n// shape, expressed purely by declaring what each step needs.\n//\n// Neither `explanation` nor `reviewNotes` is declared in any code cell. Each\n// agent cell's //@ bind: line assigns that agent's answer into this JShell\n// session as a String, so by the time this cell runs they are ordinary Java\n// variables and the two answers can be combined like any other data.\nSystem.out.println(\"--- Explanation ---\\n\" + explanation);\nSystem.out.println(\"\\n--- Review ---\\n\" + reviewNotes);",
      "output": "",
      "executed": false
    },
    {
      "id": "a501-pipe",
      "type": "PIPELINE",
      "mode": "jshell",
      "anchor": "multi-agent-review",
      "pipelineSteps": [
        "code-input",
        "explain",
        "review",
        "combine"
      ],
      "source": "//@ pipeline: Multi-Agent Review\n//@ steps: code-input, explain, review, combine",
      "output": "",
      "executed": false
    }
  ]
}
